-- title:
--   Bi-invariance of the level Hecke set under the idelic stabiliser
-- statement:
--   Fix $a,b\in\mathbb Q$ and let $\Lambda$ and $O$ be $\mathbb Z$-submodules of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$, each an order in the project's sense [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11): containing $1$, closed under multiplication, spanning $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ over $\mathbb Q$, and finitely generated over $\mathbb Z$. Assume $O\le\Lambda$, and let $\ell$ be a natural number (no primality is assumed). For a $\mathbb Z$-submodule $X$ write $\widehat X$ for [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox X`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14), the additive subgroup of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ generated by the tensors $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in X$ and $\alpha$ an everywhere-integral finite adele, and $X^{(g)}$ for [`Submodule.conjByFiniteIdele X g`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L31), the $\mathbb Z$-submodule of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ of elements whose image under $\mathrm{includeLeft}$ lies in $g\widehat Xg^{-1}$. Let $u,h$ be units of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ with $u$ in the stabiliser of the set $\widehat O$ for the multiplication action of units, and with $h$ in [`CerednikDrinfeld.levelHeckeUSet`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_ClassSetGraph.html#L44) $\Lambda\,O\,\ell$, i.e. $h\in\widehat O$, $\ell h^{-1}\in\widehat O$, $h^{-1}\notin\widehat O$, $\ell^{-1}h\notin\widehat O$, together with $O^{(h)}\neq O$ and $O\not\le\Lambda^{(h)}$. Then both $uh$ and $hu$ again lie in [`CerednikDrinfeld.levelHeckeUSet`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_ClassSetGraph.html#L44) $\Lambda\,O\,\ell$.
--
--   This is the bi-invariance of the $U_\ell$-type double coset attached to the suborder $O\le\Lambda$ under the idelic unit group $\widehat O^{\times}$, the statement that makes $\mathcal U_\ell(\Lambda,O)$ a union of double cosets for that group. It is used in the identification of this set with a single double coset of the finite idelic stabiliser and in the verification of the Hecke laws and Hecke matrices on the class set graph of the Cerednik–Drinfeld comparison.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_mul_mem_levelHeckeUSet_and_mul_mem_levelHeckeUSet_of_mem_finiteIdeleStabilizer.lean

